me(h)":72,"IC50_Dark(M*10^-6)":59,"IC50_Dark_value":59,"Method":"MTT","Notes":"72 h BOLD-100 alone. Figure label gives dispersion without specifying SD or SEM.","DOI":"10.1002/advs.202301939","Year":2023,"Counterion":"[Na+]","Type":"IC50"},{"Measurement_ID":"MCTM-982310","Abbreviation_in_the_article":"BOLD-100","Cell_line":"HCTR","Time(h)":72,"IC50_Dark(M*10^-6)":114.1,"IC50_Dark_value":114.1,"Method":"MTT","Notes":"Genetic context: HCT116 subline with acquired BOLD-100 resistance. 72 h BOLD-100 alone. Figure label gives dispersion without specifying SD or SEM.","DOI":"10.1002/advs.202301939","Year":2023,"Counterion":"[Na+]","Type":"IC50"},{"Measurement_ID":"MCTM-983901","Abbreviation_in_the_article":"BOLD-100","Cell_line":"MCF7(2)","Time(h)":72,"IC50_Dark(M*10^-6)":100,"IC50_Dark_value":100,"Method":"Crystal violet","Notes":"Author-reported approximate net-growth endpoint (≈100 µM).","DOI":"10.3390/cancers12092647","Year":2020,"Counterion":"[Na+]","Type":"GI50"},{"Measurement_ID":"MCTM-983902","Abbreviation_in_the_article":"BOLD-100","Cell_line":"MDA-MB-231","Time(h)":72,"IC50_Dark(M*10^-6)":100,"IC50_Dark_value":100,"Method":"Crystal violet","Notes":"Author-reported approximate net-growth endpoint (≈100 µM).","DOI":"10.3390/cancers12092647","Year":2020,"Counterion":"[Na+]","Type":"GI50"},{"Measurement_ID":"MCTM-983903","Abbreviation_in_the_article":"BOLD-100","Cell_line":"MDA-MB-468","Time(h)":72,"IC50_Dark(M*10^-6)":100,"IC50_Dark_value":100,"Method":"Crystal violet","Notes":"Author-reported approximate net-growth endpoint (≈100 µM).","DOI":"10.3390/cancers12092647","Year":2020,"Counterion":"[Na+]","Type":"GI50"}],"logp":[{"abbreviation_in_the_article":"KP1019","value":-0.4,"value_relation":"=","std":0.02,"type_authors":"logP","method":"shake-flask","aqueous_phase":"water","doi":"10.1002/elps.201700443","year":2018,"counterion":"c1ccc2[nH][nH+]cc2c1","record_id":"MLDB-000213","detection":"ICP-MS","method_description":"The shake flask procedure outlined previously 28, 46 was followed for the determination of solubility and log P values. A saturated solution of complex was suspended in H2O (pre-saturated with n-octanol) and shaken for 4 days on an orbital shaker. The solution was centrifuged for 5 min at 2000 rpm prior to aqueous aliquots being collected for total Ru concentration analysis, and partition experiments with n-octanol (pre-saturated with H2O) at three ratios (2:1, 1:1, and 0.5:1). After 30 min incubation time on an orbital shaker, the samples were shaken by hand for an additional 5 min and were then centrifuged at 10 000 rpm for 5 min. The aqueous layer was collected with a syringe and diluted 1:100 in 5% HNO3. The ruthenium content was measured via direct infusion through an ASX-500 autosampler (CETAC technologies) in a Serie SuSi laminar flow hood (SPECTEC) into an Agilent 7700 ICP-MS, equipped with a MicroMist nebulizer and a Scott double pass spray chamber. All analysis were carried out in triplicate unless otherwise specified."},{"abbreviation_in_the_article":"NKP-1339","value":0.27,"value_relation":"=","type_authors":"logD","method":"shake-flask","aqueous_phase":"PBS","pH":7.4,"temperature_C":25,"doi":"10.1021/acs.inorgchem.6b00359","year":2016,"counterion":"[Na+]","record_id":"MLDB-003386","detection":"UV-Vis","method_description":"Distribution coefficients (D7.4) were determined by the shake flask method (37) using n-octanol and PBS. The sodium-compensated complexes 1b, 2b, and 3b, as well as Na[RuCl4Py2], Na[RuCl4Him2], and Na[RuCl4Hind2] (NKP-1339) were dissolved in n-octanol presaturated PBS to give 200 μM solutions; 3b and NKP-1339 were dissolved in DMSO to improve solubility and then added to PBS to give a 1% DMSO solution. The aqueous solutions and n-octanol in 1:1 v/v ratio were mixed with an orbital shaker for 2 h at 25 °C. The mixtures were then centrifuged at 5000 rpm for 3 min at 25 °C. UV–vis spectra were taken at room temperature of the aqueous phase before and after shaking, and the absorbance at λmax was compared to ascertain the value of D7.4."},{"abbreviation_in_the_article":"KP1019","value":-0.6,"value_relation":"=","type_authors":"logP","method":"shake-flask","aqueous_phase":"water","temperature_C":25,"doi":"10.1007/s10534-019-00210-7","year":2019,"counterion":"c1ccc2[nH][nH+]cc2c1","record_id":"MLDB-004361","detection":"UV-Vis","method_description":"The octanol–water partition coefficients were determined by a modified shake-flask method (Cirri et al. 2017, Marzo et al. 2017). Water (250 mL, distilled after Milli-Q purification) and n-octanol (250 mL) were shaken together for 72 h to allow saturation of both phases in a 500 mL flask. The suspension was allowed to separate at least for one week in the dark. A solution of the complexes was prepared using the water phase (3 × 10-3 M) and an equal volume of octanol was added. Biphasic solutions were mixed for ten minutes and then centrifuged at 25 °C with an MPW-260R centrifuge equipped with a 11,746 rotor for 5 min at 6000 rpm to allow separation. Concentrations in both phases were determined through UV–Vis or ICP-AES spectroscopy depending on the properties of each complex. Reported logP values are defined as log10([complex]oct/[complex]wat). Final values were reported as mean of three determinations."}]}